{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013cmb2spPgN3xTvh2prJytA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient NMR Murday Cotts temperature dependence cm2/s\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy\",\"url\":\"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"link.aps.org\",\"url\":\"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302\"},{\"title\":\"MIT Libraries logoDSpace@MIT\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.mit.edu/handle/1721.1/95617\"},{\"title\":\"Study of transport processes in Li-ion electrolytes by Multi-nuclear diffusion NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/2020/09/21/study-of-transport-processes-in-li-ion-electrolytes-by-multi-nuclear-diffusion-nmr/\"},{\"title\":\"next.sciencegate.app\",\"url\":\"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return the Murday and Cotts temperature equation or its numerical coefficients, so I can't give you the specific cm²/s values from the original paper.\n\n- **Original paper:** Several reference lists cite J. S. Murday and R. M. Cotts, \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" *J. Chem. Phys.* 48:4938–4945 (1968). The search returned citations to it but not its text. (Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945)\n- **Later comparison:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study reports that its calculated self-diffusion coefficients agree well with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure, and it fits an Arrhenius form to its simulation results. (Calculated self-diffusion coefficient is in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere. We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.) That paper is Wang and Ni, *Heat Mass Transfer* 48, 253–257 (2012). I did not retrieve its fitted numbers.\n- **Solid lithium, not liquid:** A separate ⁷Li NMR study of solid lithium gives a Seeger-type expression with a prefactor of 0.038 cm²/s and an activation energy of 12.0 kcal/mol. That applies to the solid phase, so it doesn't answer your liquid-phase question. (D SD=D 10·exp(−Q 1/RT)·[1+D 21·exp(−Q 21/RT)], withD 10=0.038 cm2s−1,Q 1=12.0 kcal mol−1)\n- **Cotts group liquid-Li NMR:** One abstract describes a ⁷Li pulsed-field-gradient NMR measurement of self-diffusion in liquid lithium, compared with the Cohen–Turnbull free-volume model. I couldn't confirm its authors or year from the snippet. (The coefficient of self-diffusion of 7Li in liquid lithium has been measured with nuclear magnetic resonance. The diffusion coefficient was determined from observations of the dependence of the spin-echo signal upon the amplitude of a pulsed magnetic field gradient.)\n\nTo get the Murday–Cotts fit itself, the 1968 *J. Chem. Phys.* article is the primary source. The Wang and Ni 2012 paper is the best secondary source I found for checking it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0cb447c-5b09-4929-b8ae-4d7feb0d135b","uuid":"ace4e362-0520-4777-9750-838651beaa27","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:12:07.800Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient NMR Murday Cotts temperature dependence cm2/s","results":